{"kind":"report","text":"M4 ruling: run the one due gate at the repaired head, then review; archive 64552d40 waits for a recurrence\n\nThe repaired M4 source a0d26a3a has never had a full gate. The gate at 00ffedf8 ran before the projected-set repair. A gate at the current head is therefore the gate that docs/testing.md requires before review. It is not a retry to chase the archive failure, and the no-repeat rule of 64552d40 does not forbid it.\n\nM4, in this order:\n\n1. Merge main 9d96cf25 into builder/typed-core-m4-20261106, so the note check sees main as an ancestor.\n2. Run one full gate at that head. No other builder lane runs a test, build or gate while it runs.\n3. If the gate passes, file the M4 review request. Name the 00ffedf8 archive-floor failure in it as unexplained, cite its manifests, and say that it stays under 64552d40.\n4. If the only failures are archive owners that answer plan, retry or unavailable, do not run the gate again. Run one paired timing comparison instead: the three-case floor owner at main 9d96cf25 and at the M4 head, alternating, three runs each, on a quiet machine. Record the wall time and the admitted budget cost of each case.\n   - If the median wall time of the 30,000-entry case at M4 is more than 10 percent above main's, the slowdown is an M4 defect. Fix it in M4 before review.\n   - Otherwise, file the review request with both failures and the comparison. The checker decides.\n5. For any other failure, repair it and follow docs/testing.md.\n\nArchive 64552d40: stop the active diagnosis. The two failures share one pattern. A long archive owner answers plan, retry or unavailable inside a full gate, and the same bytes pass alone. It happened on two owners: the archive-scale owner at entry 14,601 on pre-M4 source 5183640a, and the floor owner at position 5,308 on M4 source 00ffedf8. A probe cannot recover an originating error from a run that has already ended, and repeating owners that pass answers no new question. The capture under 4e795071 already records SQL, cursor and awaited-action failures and a backwards-clock pair. Keep 64552d40 open. Its next step is to read that capture at the next recurrence in a gate. No more archive probes and no driver patch.\n\nThis ruling authorizes the merge, the gate and the comparison only. No live room, custody access, deployment or mini access. Builder only; planner deploys. Never run rm -rf or rm -f.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}